.mm/
secrets/

# Backups of .env hold live credentials. A bare `.env` rule does not
# cover .env.corrupt.bak or .env.bak-<timestamp>, which is how they once
# reached a public repo.
.env.*
!.env.example
*.bak
*.bak-*
